  "solution": {
    "text": "<br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0094_fb69929cf864.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /> <br/><br/><br/><br/>Let give small displacement to  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> . The equilibrium will be stable if net force after giving displacement will be in direction of position of equilibrium<br/><br/><br/><br/> <br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0094_7031b17cf84e.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /> <br/><br/><br/><br/> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mrow></math> <br/><br/>then net force will be directed towards vertex i.e. initial equilibrium position<br/><br/> <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mtext>  </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mrow></math> <br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> of sphere and <math><mtext> α </mtext></math> is very small<br/><br/> <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mtext>α </mtext><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>×</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>2</mn><mtext>α</mtext></math> <br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9.8</mn><mo>×</mo><mtext> </mtext><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>"
